1:# UFFP Mobile App
3:Universal Forecasting & Fermi Problems mobile application built with React Native and Expo.
5:## Overview
7:This mobile app implements probabilistic forecasting using the Tetlock methodology, allowing users to:
8:- Create and track forecasts with Monte Carlo simulations
9:- Build forecasts using triangular, normal, beta, and uniform distributions
10:- Calculate Brier scores for forecast accuracy
11:- View calibration and performance metrics
12:- Use research prompts and evidence management
14:## Features
16:- **Forecast Creation**: Build forecasts with multiple drivers and distribution types
17:- **Monte Carlo Simulation**: Run 10,000+ iterations for probabilistic outcomes
18:- **Evidence Manager**: Track research, data sources, and key findings
19:- **Calibration Tracking**: Monitor your forecasting accuracy over time
20:- **Brier Score Calculation**: Quantify forecast performance
21:- **Comparison Tools**: Compare forecasts side-by-side
22:- **Tufte-inspired Design**: Clean, information-dense visual design
24:## Tech Stack
26:- **Framework**: React Native 0.81.5
27:- **UI**: Expo 54.x
28:- **Navigation**: React Navigation 7.x
29:- **Charts**: react-native-chart-kit, react-native-svg
30:- **Language**: TypeScript 5.9
32:## Getting Started
34:### Prerequisites
36:- Node.js 18+
37:- npm or yarn
38:- Expo CLI (`npm install -g expo-cli`)
39:- iOS Simulator (Mac) or Android Emulator
41:### Installation
43:```bash
44:# Install dependencies
45:npm install
47:# Start development server
48:npm start
50:# Run on specific platform
51:npm run ios       # iOS simulator
52:npm run android   # Android emulator
53:npm run web       # Web browser
54:```
