58:```
59:├── src/
60:│   ├── components/       # Reusable UI components
61:│   ├── screens/          # Screen components
62:│   ├── services/         # Business logic (forecasting, simulation)
63:│   ├── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
64:│   ├── constants/        # Research prompts, glossary
65:│   ├── styles/           # Tufte-inspired styling
66:│   └── App.tsx           # Root component
67:├── assets/               # Images, fonts
68:├── App.tsx               # Entry point
69:└── package.json
70:```
72:## Key Components
74:### Screens
75:- **HomeScreen**: Main forecast list and leaderboard
76:- **CreateForecastScreen**: Build new forecasts with drivers
77:- **ForecastDetailScreen**: View simulation results
78:- **CompareScreen**: Compare multiple forecasts
79:- **CalibrationScreen**: Track forecasting accuracy
80:- **BrierScoreScreen**: Performance metrics
82:### Services
83:- **ForecastService**: Monte Carlo simulation engine
84:  - Triangular, normal, uniform, beta distributions
85:  - Histogram generation
86:  - Brier score calculation
88:## Documentation
90:- [Design Principles](DESIGN.md)
91:- [Quick Start Guide](QUICKSTART.md)
92:- [Agent Forecasting Guide](AGENT_FORECASTING_GUIDE.md)
93:- [Troubleshooting](TROUBLESHOOTING.md)
95:## Forecasting Methodology
97:This app implements:
98:- **Fermi Estimation**: Break down complex questions into estimatable components
99:- **Base Rates**: Ground forecasts in historical frequencies
100:- **Premortem Analysis**: Identify potential failure modes
101:- **Monte Carlo Simulation**: Probabilistic modeling with distribution parameters
102:- **Brier Scores**: Quantitative accuracy measurement
104:## Example Use Cases
106:- Forecasting company revenue (e.g., ASTS, RKLB)
107:- Market cap predictions
108:- Profitability milestones
109:- Any quantifiable future outcome
