## Critical Decisions Made

### 1. Native Rust (Not Web)
- Performance: 10K+ Monte Carlo iterations in <500ms
- GPUI: Zed-quality interface
- Cross-platform: macOS/Linux/Windows

### 2. Fermi Decomposition is Mandatory
- Not "optional justification"
- Core methodology from Tetlock research
- Drivers + evidence + simulation = forecast

### 3. CRDT Collaboration
- Real-time teams without conflicts
- Yrs library (battle-tested)
- WebRTC P2P + WebSocket fallback

### 4. Event-Sourced Versioning
- Complete time-travel
- Audit trail
- Enables learning from history

### 5. Yokai Aesthetics
- Unique visual identity
- Mnemonic (remember what each agent does)
- Playful but professional

### 6. CLI-First Interface
- Like Zed, not like web app
- Keyboard-driven
- Command language (not clicks)

