## Testing Strategy

### Test Pyramid

```
         /\
        /  \  E2E (5%)
       /----\
      /      \  Integration (15%)
     /--------\
    /          \  Unit (80%)
   /____________\
```

**Unit Tests** (80%): Fast, isolated, test pure functions
```rust
#[test]
fn test_triangular_distribution_sampling() {
    let dist = Triangular::new(0.0, 50.0, 100.0).unwrap();
    let sample = dist.sample(&mut rng);
    assert!(sample >= 0.0 && sample <= 100.0);
}
```

**Integration Tests** (15%): Test module interactions
```rust
#[test]
fn test_forecast_simulation_pipeline() {
    let forecast = parse_fpl(FPL_CODE);
    let result = simulate(&forecast, 1000);
    assert!(result.probability > 0.0 && result.probability < 1.0);
}
```

**E2E Tests** (5%): Full system with real services
```rust
#[tokio::test]
async fn test_collaborative_forecast_editing() {
    let client1 = connect_client("user1").await;
    let client2 = connect_client("user2").await;
    
    client1.edit_driver("market_tam", new_dist).await;
    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(100)).await;
    
    let forecast = client2.get_forecast().await;
    assert_eq!(forecast.drivers[0].distribution, new_dist);
}
```

### Test Commands

```bash
# Run all tests
cargo test --workspace

# Run only unit tests
cargo test --lib

# Run only integration tests
cargo test --test '*'

# Run with coverage
cargo tarpaulin --out Html --output-dir coverage/

# Run property-based tests (using proptest)
cargo test prop_test -- --nocapture

# Run benchmarks
cargo bench
```

